# tier: deterministic-repeatability
# oracle: regression pin, emulator is oracle
# Owning plan 04-23 (PKG-01, D-39): the stdout of tests/installed-consumer, built only against the
# installed, relocated package and run on build/release/images/boot-stub.exec, diag-cpu-1.ivsc, (plan 05-11)
# diag-ctrl-psg-1.ivsc and (plan 06-13) diag-stic-1.ivsc (gate step pkg-install). Self-consistent, not independent: the emulator produced these values.
# The digest.<domain> lines must also equal data/golden/diag-input-pass.digests (cross-path
# agreement with the runner); since plan 05-11 its ctrl.digest.<domain> lines and observed domains must equal
# data/golden/diag-ctrl-psg-pass.digests (the replay of diag-ctrl-psg-pass through the installed headers, the
# peeked $01FE after the first event is 0x007E, the new lines are additions only); since plan 06-13 its stic.digest.<domain>
# lines and observed domains (video and audio observed, the write log and the input not) must equal data/golden/diag-stic-fgbg-pass.digests
# (the replay of diag-stic-fgbg-pass: first slot header, hand-derived pixels, a frame-stop second pass; again additions only). The step drops these # lines before comparing. A change is a
# reviewed diff, regenerated from build/gate/pkg-consumer.txt after a gate run.
# Plan 07-09 (D-26, SCN-01) adds the fourth replay, of data/scenarios/demo-lamp-tone-pass.ivss (lines prefixed scn.), run on boot-stub-2.exec and
# lamp-tone.ivsc (gate step pkg-install): the project boot stub contract 2, the zero GROM and the original program, the six input events and the guest
# words at the four stops. Its scn.digest.<domain> lines and observed domains (all nine: video, audio, input and the write log observed) must equal
# data/golden/demo-lamp-tone-pass.digests; the new lines are additions only.
